      "role": "input"
    }
  ],
  "components": [
    {
      "ref": "D1",
      "kind": "diode",
      "value": "1N4007",
      "package": "axial_diode",
      "pins": {
        "A": "AC1",
        "K": "VDC"
      },
      "notes": "Conducts on the half-cycle where AC1 is positive."
    },
    {
      "ref": "D2",
      "kind": "diode",
      "value": "1N4007",
      "package": "axial_diode",
      "pins": {
        "A": "AC2",
        "K": "VDC"
      }
    },
    {
      "ref": "D3",
      "kind": "diode",
      "value": "1N4007",
      "package": "axial_diode",
      "pins": {
        "A": "GND",
        "K": "AC1"
      }
    },
    {
      "ref": "D4",
      "kind": "diode",
      "value": "1N4007",
      "package": "axial_diode",
      "pins": {
        "A": "GND",
        "K": "AC2"
      }
    },
    {
      "ref": "C1",
      "kind": "polarized_capacitor",
      "value": "470uF",
      "package": "radial_electrolytic",
      "pins": {
        "+": "VDC",
        "-": "GND"
      },
      "notes": "Smoothing cap. Backwards is the classic way to make one vent."
    },
    {
      "ref": "RL",
      "kind": "resistor",
      "value": "1k",
      "pins": {
        "1": "VDC",
        "2": "GND"
      },
      "notes": "Bleeder / load."
    },
    {
      "ref": "R1",
      "kind": "resistor",
      "value": "330",
      "pins": {
        "1": "VDC",
        "2": "LEDA"
      }
    },
    {
      "ref": "LED1",
      "kind": "led",
      "value": "red 5mm",
      "package": "led_5mm",
      "pins": {
        "A": "LEDA",
        "K": "GND"
      },
      "notes": "Power-on indicator."
    }
  ],
  "warnings": [
    "Wave generator only — never wire this to mains. The four diodes all face the same way round the loop, which is the part that is easy to get wrong.",
    "Earth ground: most bench generators and scopes tie their ground clips to mains earth. The generator's ground goes on AC2 here, not on GND, so don't also clip a scope's ground to GND: through earth that shorts D4. Measure VDC with a handheld meter, or keep the scope's ground clip on AC2 and use two probes: VDC minus GND. Expect VDC a little under 10 V − 1.4 V, since a 50 Ω generator sags under the 1 kΩ load and the LED."
  ],
  "sources": [
